ing their education is of the  utmost importance so the girls still  live at home with their parents but  during an interview with the New York  Times the girls did state that they  spend as much time at hype house as they  can mark and Heidi who are almost famous  tick tock stars have a set of rules they  want their daughters to follow but they  don't want to infringe on their creative  freedom during the same interview mark D  Emilio revealed that as parents one  thing they say all the time is that this  is just about creating options for their  kids mark also admitted that while he  doesn't know where this whole hype house  thing is going he hopes that his  daughters can do what they love and most  importantly be happy as long as their  girls sleep at home at night and go to  school in the morning the D'Amelio  are happy my family's my support system  I know that they all have my back  Charlie D Emilio might be hype houses  youngest tick tock star but she's also  the tick talker with the most followers  the 15 year old has over 34 million  followers on the platform whereas her 18  year old sister Dixie has about 14  million the sisters are pros when it  comes to producing daily videos and  that's a good thing considering that  hype House members are obliged to  turnout daily content if House members  fail to respect this role they can get  kicked out of hype house in the blink of  an eye charlie is famous for her  lip-syncing and choreographed dance  videos and Dixie is well known for her  similar dance style and comedic videos  the girls don't seem to have any issues  juggling their schoolwork and content  creation duties so they're in the clear  for now but wait what happens when a  House member fails to upload daily  content  well according to Thomas if someone  slips up constantly they won't be a part  of the team anymore  Thomas also stated that tick talkers  can't come and stay with them for a week  and not make any videos so we want to be  putting out a couple videos a week of  groups  tik-tok is especially popular with  people under 18 years old so when  creating hype house chase Hudson aka lil  hoodie and Thomas knew that they had to  stay on trend with her brand to hold on  to their popularity chase Thomas and the  creator collective hype house are signed  with WME and to remain in good standing  with WME they have to uphold the hype  house's stellar reputation getting into  trouble with the cops or giving hype  house a bad reputation can put them in  hot waters with the agency so their  brand is their bond it doesn't matter  how many followers a person has certain  rules need to be followed especially  since the agency has contracts with  minors that's why the party culture is  so frowned upon at hype house thomas  revealed that partying is not in line  with anyone in the houses brand the D  Emilio sisters have to be on their best  behavior to prevent fans from boycotting  them can you imagine what would happen  if a bunch of teenagers moved in to hide  house without having a set of golden  rules to follow yeah it would be anarchy  luckily everything has been carefully  planned to protect the collaborators  rights while maintaining a friendly and  productive atmosphere unlike Jake Paul's  team 10 the members of hype house aren't  made to allocate a portion of their  earnings to a head honcho  however they are expected to replace  something if they break or damage it for  the most part the hype house residents  aren't nearly as destructive as team 10  so maintaining the mansion's current  state hasn't been a problem Jake Paul  was sued for two million dollars for  trashing the team ten house so just in  case history repeats itself hype how has  added a you break you buy role to their  contract if someone breaks something  they have a total of 15 days to replace  it you know we argue we fight we have  our differences but the end of the day  we all go to bed we still love each  other  Thomas was inspired to create hype house  after spending time in the team 10  mansion he quickly realized that having  popular tick stalkers in one place could  boost views in a matter of seconds so we  got to work recruiting some of the  biggest tick tock errs on the platform  Thomas and chase decided to run out a  huge LA mansion with 20 other tick tock  errs which made running a room very  affordable most of the House members do  not live in the mansion full-time but  they run a room for about $900 a month  they're free to come and go as they  please as long as they create daily  content while ensuring to be present on  collab days collab days are super  important for hype House members  appearing in each other's videos and  creating new content for the hype house  tick tock page helps everyone involved  get more followers and views members are  expected to promote each other creating  organic growth in the process Thomas  told Forbes that Charlie Dee Emilio  changed the tick tock app by uploading  dance videos with her help everyone at  hype house is creating new and fun  dances that bring in loads of traffic  we're just trying to push each other as  best we can when you're on the outside  looking in  hi pops can come off as a place where  teens go to throw blowout parties but  that's the opposite of what hype house  is about when you're on the inside  looking out it's clear that the mansion  is a place of business where like-minded  people go to create content for their  slew of fans where as Charlie and  Dixie's parents are free to come and go  as they please the girls still need to  get permission before inviting some of  their friends over high-pass creators  and investors want to make sure that the  group members are respecting the rules  and they also want to ensure that their  stars are well protected  so the gated community only opens for  visitors who have been approved ahead of  time tons of new faces head to hype  house on collab days but these visitors  are there to have fun and be themselves  while creating tick tock videos if Dixie  and Charlie want to hang out with their  friends they're better off doing it at  home  a little way I am when cheese Hudson  decided to create hype house he  immediately contacted the D Emilio  sisters because their brand was so on  point these two social media stars got  to where they are today by being  themselves they're all about embracing  their inner weirdness and connecting  with fans through relatable content so  when chase approaches new collaborators  he keeps authenticity in mind he wants  everyone at the hype house to bring  something new to the table and as long  as they're respectful and have plenty of  followers pretty much anything goes  chases the group scout and according to  Cosmopolitan he's looking for people who  are talented weird funny or extremely  good-looking  luckily for Charlie and Dixie they check  all of these boxes hype House members  could potentially lose their spot if  they stopped being true to themselves  and mislead their fans viewers want  original content so copying others just  isn't an option keep posting keep going  you're gonna you're gonna do big things  in life you just can't focus on what  they have to say the tic-tock world is  super competitive but typically accounts  that have the most followers get the  most views the members of hype house are  scared to get comfortable and lose  stamina they want their follower base to  keep growing every single day so to grow  their accounts pipe House members  collaborate with different tick talkers  every single week and so far charlie has  managed to bring in around 200,000 new  followers every single day everyone at  hype house is encouraged to attend  tik-tok events where they can connect  with their fans while inspiring new ones  to follow them attending huge events  like YouTube's VidCon party is a must  fans will be lining up to meet Charlie  and Dixie as well as other members of  the hype house at the 2020 VidCon eve